  "notes": [
    "Promotion to new-hand multi-seed scaling requires the replication itself to have pooled delta >0, >=2/3 positive anchors, Standard10 >=0, both seats >=0, caps/base/schedule valid, and robust positive worst alignment on >=75% of steps; then both cohorts will be meta-aggregated before promotion. Failure is evidence against this 32-step formulation, not proof that all long-horizon multi-objective learning is impossible.",
    "Raw second-cohort SHA256 be20c76173b078e11e0994f410e025cdc2d0a66fe7d91c7d5092d9cf192d290b; exact meta-analysis verified zero deck overlap with the first cohort. Across 6,144 independent matched pairs / 24,576 hands, pooled +3.906820 bb/100 CI[-5.579604,13.393243], every anchor point and both seat points were positive."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "The independent seed-20261390 cohort reproduced the MGDA mechanism on 32/32 steps and passed every policy-direction gate: treatment-control was +6.616 Standard10, +13.246 Slumbot-free, +1.900 CFR96, pooled +7.254 CI[-2.396,16.905], with both seats positive. Two-cohort raw aggregation had zero deck overlap and pooled +3.907 CI[-5.580,13.393], all three anchors and both seats positive.",
    "conclusion": "Conflict-aware residual learning now has two-seed mechanism replication and positive combined breadth, while uncertainty remains large and the first cohort alone was mixed. This justifies a modest new-hand multi-seed scale to estimate a geometric learning curve and preservation, not a Slumbot test or a claim of established strength.",
    "decision": "ADMIT_MODEST_NEW_HAND_MULTI_SEED_SCALE",
    "next_step": "Collect multiple fresh on-policy cohorts at a modest geometric dose, retaining Standard10 frozen-base/cap protection and matched ordinary controls. Evaluate checkpoint doses on untouched common decks; escalate only if slopes, multi-seed breadth, both seats, and Standard10 preservation remain directionally aligned."
  },
